# Dire Blunderbuss's granted ability, "you may sacrifice an artifact other than Dire Blunderbuss. When you do, this
# creature deals damage equal to its power to target creature." On turn three Bot1 declines (an empty choice): nothing is
# sacrificed and no reflexive ability triggers (CR 603.12), so no target is asked for. On turn five the attacking
# Ornithopter, an artifact itself, is the artifact sacrificed: the reflexive ability still triggers, and the creature
# deals damage equal to its power as it last existed on the battlefield, 3 with the Blunderbuss's +3/+0 (the card's
# ruling, CR 608.2h), killing Bot2's Ornithopter, the one creature left to target. Bot2's Ornithopter attacking on turn
# four is no attack of "this creature": nothing triggers then. The sacrificed attacker deals no combat damage.

